# Rank 1027 / CVE-2022-20619 (SECURITY-2467): the Bitbucket branch source
# plugin's doFillRepositoryItems form method is reachable by GET. It resolves
# stored Jenkins credentials for a caller-supplied serverUrl and then calls the
# Bitbucket API with them, so a crafted page could make a victim's browser
# drive a connection to an attacker's server carrying those credentials
# (CWE-352). The fixed revision adds a single annotation, @RequirePOST.
#
# ATTENTION, precision cost, measured, plus a concept that does not reach it.
#
# The naive rule is "a Stapler form method without @RequirePOST". This plugin
# has 19 doFill, doCheck and doTest methods, and even after the security fix
# exactly 1 carries the annotation, so that rule would report 19 sites for one
# true positive here. The other 18 are deliberately left alone because they
# neither connect out nor change state, which is what the Jenkins guidance
# actually asks about.
#
# The right discriminator is narrower: the method resolves credentials and then
# performs a remote call with them, which is what separates
# doFillRepositoryItems from its sibling doFillCredentialsIdItems, left
# unannotated in the same class because it only lists local credential ids. The
# remote half is plugin-specific naming (BitbucketApiFactory.newInstance,
# getTeam, getRepositories), and expressing "calls out through some client
# object" needs argument-to-call pairing the flat feature bag does not provide,
# the same limit ranks 1017 and 1022 hit. No Jenkins corpus is available here
# beyond this one plugin, so a narrower credentials-plus-remote-call binding
# cannot be measured for precision and none is written.
#
# The existing concept misses this twice over.
# code.JenkinsCredentialEndpointMissingPostPermission (VYQL-AUTH-073, CWE-862
# and CWE-352) describes the weakness well, but its binding is pinned to the
# method names doCreateApiToken, doCheckRepoAccess and doTestGithubAccess, and
# it also requires the absence of checkPermission or hasPermission. This method
# performs both an Item.EXTENDED_READ and a CredentialsProvider.USE_ITEM check;
# the permissions are never the problem, only the missing POST requirement.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-precision-cost

test "rank1027: form method resolves credentials and calls out with no POST requirement"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/com/cloudbees/jenkins/plugins/bitbucket/BitbucketSCMSource.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-073
  code
  ```
  public static class DescriptorImpl extends SCMSourceDescriptor {
      @SuppressWarnings("unused") // used By stapler
      public ListBoxModel doFillRepositoryItems(@AncestorInPath SCMSourceOwner context,
                                                @QueryParameter String serverUrl,
                                                @QueryParameter String credentialsId,
                                                @QueryParameter String repoOwner)
              throws IOException, InterruptedException {
          if (context != null && !context.hasPermission(Item.EXTENDED_READ)) {
              return new ListBoxModel();
          }
          if (context != null && !context.hasPermission(CredentialsProvider.USE_ITEM)) {
              return new ListBoxModel();
          }

          StandardCredentials credentials = BitbucketCredentials.lookupCredentials(
                  serverUrl, context, credentialsId, StandardCredentials.class);
          BitbucketAuthenticator authenticator = AuthenticationTokens.convert(
                  BitbucketAuthenticator.authenticationContext(serverUrl), credentials);

          BitbucketApi bitbucket = BitbucketApiFactory.newInstance(serverUrl, authenticator, repoOwner, null);
          BitbucketTeam team = bitbucket.getTeam();
          ListBoxModel result = new ListBoxModel();
          for (BitbucketRepository repo : bitbucket.getRepositories(null)) {
              result.add(repo.getRepositoryName());
          }
          return result;
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1027: fix requires POST on the same form method"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/com/cloudbees/jenkins/plugins/bitbucket/BitbucketSCMSource.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-073
  code
  ```
  public static class DescriptorImpl extends SCMSourceDescriptor {
      @SuppressWarnings("unused") // used By stapler
      @RequirePOST
      public ListBoxModel doFillRepositoryItems(@AncestorInPath SCMSourceOwner context,
                                                @QueryParameter String serverUrl,
                                                @QueryParameter String credentialsId,
                                                @QueryParameter String repoOwner)
              throws IOException, InterruptedException {
          if (context != null && !context.hasPermission(Item.EXTENDED_READ)) {
              return new ListBoxModel();
          }
          if (context != null && !context.hasPermission(CredentialsProvider.USE_ITEM)) {
              return new ListBoxModel();
          }

          StandardCredentials credentials = BitbucketCredentials.lookupCredentials(
                  serverUrl, context, credentialsId, StandardCredentials.class);
          BitbucketAuthenticator authenticator = AuthenticationTokens.convert(
                  BitbucketAuthenticator.authenticationContext(serverUrl), credentials);

          BitbucketApi bitbucket = BitbucketApiFactory.newInstance(serverUrl, authenticator, repoOwner, null);
          BitbucketTeam team = bitbucket.getTeam();
          ListBoxModel result = new ListBoxModel();
          for (BitbucketRepository repo : bitbucket.getRepositories(null)) {
              result.add(repo.getRepositoryName());
          }
          return result;
      }
  }
  ```
